{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Simplifying Rational Expressions.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Simplifying Rational Expressions.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"simplifying rational expressions simplifying rational expressions","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Simplifying Rational Expressions.md","fileName":"Simplifying Rational Expressions.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Simplifying Rational Expressions","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Polynomial and Rational Expressions]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial and Rational Expressions","Rational Expression","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Simplifying Rational Expressions.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Simplifying Rational Expressions.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"simplifying rational expressions simplifying rational expressions","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Simplifying Rational Expressions.md","fileName":"Simplifying Rational Expressions.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Simplifying Rational Expressions","heading":"Simplifying Rational Expressions","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Simplifying a [[Rational Expression]] rewrites its numerator and denominator as products and cancels common nonzero factors. For example,\n\n$$\\frac{x^2-1}{x^2-2x+1}=\\frac{(x-1)(x+1)}{(x-1)^2}=\\frac{x+1}{x-1}.$$\n\nOnly complete factors can be cancelled; terms connected by addition cannot be removed independently. Values that made the original denominator zero remain excluded after simplification. The factored form therefore reveals both cancellation opportunities and domain restrictions.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Polynomial and Rational Expressions","Rational Expression","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pa